MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
A macro-time test can ask which class a piece of text belongs to.
MCDEF CLASSIFY; AS <MCGO L1 IF %A1. BC N
MCGO L2 IF %A1. BC L
MCGO L3 IF %A1. BC I
%A1. is none of them<>MCGO L0
%L1.%A1. is a number<>MCGO L0
%L2.%A1. is letters<>MCGO L0
%L3.%A1. is an identifier>
CLASSIFY 1234;
CLASSIFY -17;
CLASSIFY +0;
CLASSIFY ABC;
CLASSIFY A1;
CLASSIFY 1A;
CLASSIFY a-b;
The two equality tests are different: one compares text and the
other compares numbers.
MCSET P1=7
MCGO L1 IF 007 EN 7
they are not numerically equal<>MCGO L2
%L1.007 and 7 are numerically equal
%L2.MCGO L3 IF 007 = 7
007 and 7 are not the same characters
%L3.done
